  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-18T20:46:26.302Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be absolutely fantastic to define the location of a physical chair in your chaperone/guardian boundary area. \n\nHere's how I would personally implement it: \n\n1) make it appear in vrchat with a distance shader at a user defined position. \n\n2) Provide a few simple options: \n\na. Seat type: (couch, laz-e-boy type, desk chair, beanbag/moon chair, or simply floor. - have a simple model for it. \n\nb. player sets height of seat, \n & location and angle of backrest. \n\n3) here's the magic:  \n\nwhen VRC_Chair object is interacted: default the avatar to the idle character animation controller that you go into when the system menu/VR Dashboard is pressed. (idle standing with arms at side). \n\nTHEN: Grey the room slightly and highlight your defined chair location. When the user sits in the chair (or the ground) and confirms - sit the user's avatar and adjust world height without ipd scaling for the new headset position height. As soon as they get up, adjust back. \n\n- I already do this in a janky workaround way by moving my character to my chair which I have defined inside my steamVR chaperone bounds as a wall that sticks out; then sitting first before I click the chair object. That often doesn't work the way I would expect, a system like the above would be AMAZING.",
